Affine charts and their inverse cross-multiplication: 40 complete residue-ring polynomial identities, a=2..9, n=1..5.
Integral lattice: incidence deleted-row minors each have one signed matching and determinant +/-1; Cauchy–Binet gives det=(-1)^(a-1)*a*n^(a-1), a=2..9,n=1..5.
Deck permutation: 64 cases b,c=1..8, gcd(b,c) invariant-labelled orbits each of length bc/gcd(b,c).
WP normalization identity: 35 exact grid values with separate degree (4,6).
WP differential minors by first-order dual algebra: 15 exact values with separate degree (2,4), giving (-3 y^2 t^2,4 y t^4,2t), hence ideal (t).
WQ affine inverse: exact Laurent dictionary substitution z=y^-2*x^2-y^-3 gives y*x^2-z*y^3=1.
WQ conductor: on all exponent pairs 0..16, testing {h,ht} gives (y) on the umbrella and (y^2) for the union; the planar component ideal is (x^2).
WO normalization equations agree under (y,t)->(yt,y,t^3) and (u,v,w)->(v,w,u^2) on v^2=u*w.
Positive weights: (n+1,a,a) has degree a(n+1), and (b+c,a,a) has degree a(b+c).
All results are exact. Universal geometric, degree-bound, and all-exponent arguments are in the derivations; finite parameter runs are not substituted for them.
